// EXPECT: PASS
// Phase-7 native-authoritative demo: a pure-integer contract the NATIVE QF_BV solver proves by
// itself. Under `ANUBIS_NATIVE_AUTHORITATIVE=1` with z3 absent from PATH, this file still checks
// green — the machine-checked native pipeline (parse → bit-blast → CDCL) carries the proof. In the
// default mode it proves identically via z3, so the two configurations must agree (the equivalence
// gate asserts exactly that).
pub fn clamp_add(x: u32, y: u32) -> u32
    requires(x <= 1000)
    requires(y <= 1000)
    ensures(result >= x)
    ensures(result <= 2000)
{
    return x + y;
}

fn main() {
    // The z3-free proof this fixture demonstrates is clamp_add's CONTRACT — its `ensures`, for ALL u32
    // inputs — discharged natively from {bvadd, bvsle, bvsge}, every one a MACHINE-CHECKED blast
    // (rippleCarry_spec + sle/ule/slt/ult_correct). That is the proof-backed native-authoritative
    // fragment (`solver/src/fragment.rs`) in action with z3 off the PATH.
    //
    // A concrete call like `clamp_add(700, 300)` is deliberately omitted: it would add a u32 literal
    // coercion check that lowers to `bvand`, whose blast is not yet in the proven fragment, so it would
    // DEFER to z3 (fail-closed when z3 is absent). `bvand`/bitwise are the next fragment-widening proof.
    print(0);
}
